      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Nour Alblooshi",
      "description": "Abu Dhabi, the capital city of the United Arab Emirates, is known for its fascinating landscapes, and one of its unique natural attractions is the salt lake, also known as the Al Samha Salt Lake.\nThe Abu Dhabi salt lake is located in the Al Samha area, which is situated in the western region of Abu Dhabi, close to the border with Dubai. It is a shallow lake characterized by its high salinity, hence the name \"salt lake.\" The lake covers a significant area and is surrounded by vast expanses of salt flats, creating a mesmerizing and otherworldly environment.\n\nThe salt lake owes its formation to the arid climate and the presence of underground water sources that carry minerals and salt deposits to the surface. Over time, as the water evaporates, it leaves behind a crust of crystallized salt, giving the lake its distinct appearance.",
